{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBatteryVacuity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBatteryVacuity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.ambiguous_multisets_are_d_and_neutrino","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.ambiguous_multisets_are_d_and_neutrino","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L181-L186","doc":"The `d` quark and the neutrino each admit two multisets, matching the\nchapter's reported residual ambiguity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.unique_multisets_are_u_and_electron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.unique_multisets_are_u_and_electron","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L173-L179","doc":"The two \"uniquely determined\" multisets are exactly the two totals that\nhappen to admit a single multiset: `Σt = 2` for the `u` quark and\n`Σt = -3` for the electron.  Uniqueness is a fact about representing `2`\nand `-3` as a sum of three elements of `{-1,0,1}`, not about the framework. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.survivor_count_is_multiset_counting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.survivor_count_is_multiset_counting","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L159-L171","doc":"**The survivor count is pure multiset counting.**\n\nThe spectrum battery fixes `T = 3Q` per flavour, so each flavour is\nfiltered *independently* by one linear equation.  For\n`(u, d, νₑ, e⁻)` the required totals are `3Q = (2, -1, 0, -3)`, giving\n`1, 2, 2, 1` admissible multisets — and `1 · 2 · 2 · 1 = 4`, the reported\nsurvivor count.  `10⁴` was never cut down by a joint condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.withSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.withSum","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L155-L157","doc":"Multisets whose total twist is `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.twistMultisets_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.twistMultisets_card","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L151-L153","doc":"There are ten of them, so the four-flavour assignment space has\n`10⁴ = 10000` elements -- the figure the chapter quotes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.twistMultisets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.twistMultisets","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L145-L149","doc":"The ten multisets of three strand twists drawn from `{-1, 0, +1}`,\nlisted as sorted triples.  This is the per-flavour candidate space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.neutron_second_clause_redundant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.neutron_second_clause_redundant","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L135-L141","doc":"Same for the neutron clause: `2·(T_n/3 + 1/2) = 1` clears to `T_n = 0`,\nits own first clause. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.nucleon_second_clause_redundant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.nucleon_second_clause_redundant","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L123-L133","doc":"**The nucleon check tests one condition twice.**\n\nAs implemented the proton clause is `T_p/3 = 1 ∧ 2·(T_p/3 - 1/2) = 1`.\nCleared of denominators the second clause is `2T_p - 3 = 3`, i.e. `T_p = 3`\n— identical to the first.  The apparent two-part Gell-Mann--Nishijima check\nis a single equation stated twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.nucleon_totals_are_three_and_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.nucleon_totals_are_three_and_zero","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L115-L121","doc":"Specialised to the physical first-generation charges `3Q_u = 2`,\n`3Q_d = -1`: the proton total is `3` and the neutron total is `0`, which are\nprecisely the two values the implemented nucleon check tests for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.nucleon_totals_entailed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.nucleon_totals_entailed","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L102-L113","doc":"**The nucleon check filters nothing.**\n\nThe proton is `uud` and the neutron `udd`, so their total twists are\n`T_p = 2T_u + T_d` and `T_n = T_u + 2T_d`, while their charges are\n`Q_p = 2Q_u + Q_d` and `Q_n = Q_u + 2Q_d`.  If the spectrum battery holds\nfor the quarks (`T = 3Q` each), then `T = 3Q` holds for the nucleons\nautomatically -- by charge additivity alone.  No assignment surviving the\nspectrum battery can fail the nucleon battery. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.spectrum_independent_of_isospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.spectrum_independent_of_isospin","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L92-L98","doc":"The isospin term is irrelevant to the battery: for *any* two isospin\nvalues the criterion is unchanged.  This is why the battery tests nothing\nabout `I₃`, only about the total twist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.spectrum_iff_total_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.TwistBattery.spectrum_iff_total_twist","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/TwistBatteryVacuity.lean#L76-L90","doc":"**The spectrum battery is exactly `T = 3Q`.**\n\nBoth the candidate `Y_t = 2(Q_twist - I₃)` and the Standard-Model value\n`Y_SM = 2(Q - I₃)` carry the same `-2I₃` term, so requiring them equal\ncancels the isospin entirely.  Stated in the cleared `3×` normalisation\n(`threeQ = 3Q`, `T` the total twist, `twoI₃ = 2I₃`), where the candidate\nreads `Y_t = (2T - 3·twoI₃)/3` and the target `Y = (2·threeQ - 3·twoI₃)/3`;\nclearing the common denominator and the common `I₃` term leaves `2T = 2·threeQ`.\n\nNo characteristic or field hypothesis: this is `ℤ`-linear. ","signatureChunk":0}]}